WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:49.990 --> 00:01:52.190
[ROBIN]
Stop it, Saul! You're scaring me!

3
00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:55.010
[SAUL]
Hope you're ready 'cause
if you make an enemy

4
00:01:55.010 --> 00:02:01.180
outta me there's gonna be hell to pay!

5
00:01:56.890 --> 00:02:00.850
<b>Declaration of War</b>

6
00:02:10.820 --> 00:02:11.890
[MARINE]
What's going on?

7
00:02:11.890 --> 00:02:14.190
[MARINE]
It's Vice Admiral Saul!

8
00:02:14.190 --> 00:02:17.800
He ran away with Nico Olvia
and now he's attacking us!

9
00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:19.980
He's lost his mind!

10
00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:21.410
[MARINE]
What's he doing on Ohara?

11
00:02:21.410 --> 00:02:22.880
[MARINE]
Hell if I know!

12
00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:27.890
[SCHOLARS]
The whole island is done for!

13
00:02:27.890 --> 00:02:29.350
They're gonna burn it to the ground!

14
00:02:29.350 --> 00:02:30.990
[SCHOLARS]
Don't give up yet!

15
00:02:30.990 --> 00:02:34.660
Even if the library burns,
we can still save the books!

16
00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:36.930
Throw them out the window
and drop them in the lake!

17
00:02:36.930 --> 00:02:40.200
They're better off wet than
burned to ash! Hurry up!

18
00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:43.490
[MARINE]
Fire!

19
00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:51.760
[ROBIN]
Come back! Don't do this!
It's not like you!

20
00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:53.790
[SCHOLARS]
Get all the books out of the library!

21
00:02:53.790 --> 00:02:55.660
Don't give up on a single book!

22
00:02:55.660 --> 00:02:58.190
Don't give up on a single sentence!

23
00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:03.070
[NICO OLIVIA]
These words have been passed
on for thousands of years!

24
00:03:03.070 --> 00:03:05.570
[DR. CLOVER]
They must reach the future!

25
00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:11.210
[DR. CLOVER]
Robin! Get the heck outta here!

26
00:03:11.210 --> 00:03:13.510
The evacuation ship's gonna leave without you!

27
00:03:13.510 --> 00:03:16.800
Don't worry about me, just run!

28
00:03:51.170 --> 00:03:53.300
[ROBIN]
Mommy!

29
00:03:57.960 --> 00:03:59.860
[MARINE]
Shoot him down!

30
00:04:00.860 --> 00:04:03.030
C'mon! Go! Get moving!

31
00:04:03.030 --> 00:04:05.800
Don't you remember
what your mom told you?

32
00:04:06.630 --> 00:04:09.260
You must live, Robin!

33
00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:13.220
[MARINE]
Attention evacuees,
the ship is leaving!

34
00:04:13.220 --> 00:04:15.820
[WOMAN]
Wait! Someone's coming!

35
00:04:15.820 --> 00:04:16.790
It's her!

36
00:04:16.790 --> 00:04:20.380
[BOY]
Isn't that the monster girl?

37
00:04:20.380 --> 00:04:21.160
[BOY]
Yeah, it is!

38
00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:23.160
[BOY]
Go away! You're creepy!

39
00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:24.780
[MAN]
Hey! Now's not the time for that!

40
00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:25.750
[MAN]
No wait!

41
00:04:25.750 --> 00:04:27.750
That kid's mother Olvia
was in the newspaper

42
00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:28.650
just the other day!

43
00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:31.320
That means she's the
daughter of a criminal!

44
00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:32.410
[MAN]
You're right!

45
00:04:32.410 --> 00:04:34.310
If we let her on the ship,
it might cause us trouble!

46
00:04:34.310 --> 00:04:35.240
Just leave her!

47
00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:37.010
[MAN]
Don't be ridiculous!
She's just a child!

48
00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:38.480
Hurry up and help her!

49
00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:41.720
[SPANDINE]
Everyone stop!
Don't let that brat on board!

50
00:04:41.720 --> 00:04:42.920
[MAN]
Huh?

51
00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:45.540
She may be a child, but
she's still an archaeologist.

52
00:04:45.540 --> 00:04:47.690
That means she's a criminal
like the rest of them!

53
00:04:47.690 --> 00:04:50.930
A little girl like that?
If you say so, Chief.

54
00:04:50.930 --> 00:04:52.530
[MAN]
See? I told you!

55
00:04:52.530 --> 00:04:54.730
Good thing we didn't let her on!

56
00:04:54.730 --> 00:04:58.880
[SAUL]
Robin! Must be CP9.
Damn! I'll show them!

57
00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:01.620
[MARINE]
Chief! Vice Admiral Saul
is coming this way!

58
00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:03.340
Is that so?

59
00:05:03.340 --> 00:05:06.080
Then there was no need to question
Olvia about him after all!

60
00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:08.480
Fire! Now! Shoot him down!

61
00:05:11.240 --> 00:05:14.680
[KUZAN]
Ice Block! Partisan!

62
00:05:17.910 --> 00:05:19.550
Saul!

63
00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:28.730
[SAUL]
It's Kuzan!

64
00:05:29.730 --> 00:05:30.700
You.

65
00:05:30.700 --> 00:05:33.500
[KUZAN]
My my my. This just won't do.

66
00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:38.540
If we let a former marine stop the Buster
Call, we'd look like damn fools.

67
00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:40.910
[SAUL]
Kuzan, wake up.

68
00:05:40.910 --> 00:05:43.780
You can't tell me
this nonsense is justice!

69
00:05:43.780 --> 00:05:45.450
Pull back! Now!

70
00:05:45.450 --> 00:05:47.050
You know this ain't right!

71
00:05:47.050 --> 00:05:50.090
They're just making
an example out of Ohara!

72
00:05:50.090 --> 00:05:53.760
Come on. Please.
You're better than this.

73
00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:56.860
[KUZAN]
If it's for the good of
the world, it has to be done.

74
00:05:56.860 --> 00:06:00.600
You can't deny that those scholars
are breaking the law, can you?

75
00:06:00.600 --> 00:06:03.270
I won't criticize
your sense of justice.

76
00:06:03.270 --> 00:06:07.100
There are as many rights and wrongs
as there are viewpoints in the world.

77
00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:13.710
However, if you insist on getting in our
way, I can't sit back and do nothing.

78
00:06:21.930 --> 00:06:23.860
The evacuation ship was blown up!

79
00:06:23.860 --> 00:06:25.490
Wha...what happened?

80
00:06:25.490 --> 00:06:27.740
[MARINE]
Looked like cannon fire!
From one of our ships!

81
00:06:27.740 --> 00:06:30.370
[MARINE]
It was Vice Admiral Sakazuki!

82
00:06:31.370 --> 00:06:32.770
That idiot.

83
00:06:32.770 --> 00:06:35.510
[SAKAZUKI]
If we're doing this,
we have to be thorough.

84
00:06:32.960 --> 00:06:36.380
<b>Vice Admiral Sakazuki
Marine Headquarters
(Later to Become
Admiral Akainu)</b>

85
00:06:35.510 --> 00:06:38.410
If even one of those scholars
had managed to sneak onboard

86
00:06:38.410 --> 00:06:42.630
that ship then all the sacrifices
we made today would be in vain.

87
00:06:42.630 --> 00:06:46.730
However small, we cannot
allow any evil to thrive.

88
00:06:46.730 --> 00:06:49.030
Is this what you call justice?

89
00:06:49.030 --> 00:06:51.460
Can you take pride
in something like this?

90
00:06:51.460 --> 00:06:52.300
We went too far.

91
00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:54.370
I would never do something like that!

92
00:06:54.370 --> 00:06:56.500
[SAUL]
We gotta run, Robin!

93
00:06:56.500 --> 00:06:59.370
This fella's way too
strong for me to fight!

94
00:06:59.370 --> 00:07:00.170
[MARINE]
Saul is escaping!

95
00:07:00.170 --> 00:07:02.800
He's taking one of
the scholars with him!

96
00:07:05.230 --> 00:07:08.400
[KUZAN]
Ice Time Capsule!

97
00:07:11.090 --> 00:07:13.330
Oh no! Saul, are you okay?

98
00:07:15.860 --> 00:07:19.860
[SAUL]
Robin, you gotta get out of here.

99
00:07:22.830 --> 00:07:25.000
Don't look back, just go!

100
00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:27.740
If you stay on this island, you'll die!

101
00:07:27.740 --> 00:07:29.950
Take my raft and go out to sea!

102
00:07:29.950 --> 00:07:31.220
But what about you?

103
00:07:31.220 --> 00:07:36.930
[SAUL]
He's got me, little lady. I'm
afraid this is the end. Hurry!

104
00:07:36.930 --> 00:07:39.630
No! Everybody I care about is here!

105
00:07:39.630 --> 00:07:41.270
Now you listen to me.

106
00:07:42.230 --> 00:07:44.540
You may be lonely at first.

107
00:07:44.540 --> 00:07:48.710
But one day, you'll find true friends.

108
00:07:51.180 --> 00:07:52.180
True friends?

109
00:07:52.180 --> 00:07:56.810
Yeah, the sea's a vast
place, so I guarantee...

110
00:07:58.020 --> 00:08:01.450
someday you'll find friends
who won't ever leave you!

111
00:08:01.450 --> 00:08:06.690
No matter who you are, ain't no one
born into this world to be alone!

112
00:08:09.620 --> 00:08:10.850
[SAUL]
It's time to go, Robin.

113
00:08:10.850 --> 00:08:15.020
This is goodbye! When things
are bad, do like I taught cha.

114
00:08:15.020 --> 00:08:16.990
You remember the laugh, don'tcha?

115
00:08:16.990 --> 00:08:18.360
Look out! He's behind you!

116
00:08:18.360 --> 00:08:22.030
[SAUL]
Dereshishishishi!

117
00:08:22.030 --> 00:08:23.860
Now. Ice Time.

118
00:08:25.670 --> 00:08:26.400
Saul, no!

119
00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:28.840
Dereshishi...

120
00:08:28.840 --> 00:08:32.210
[SAUL]
Your friends are out there
at sea waiting for you, Robin.

121
00:08:32.210 --> 00:08:35.170
All you gotta do is find them!

122
00:08:38.020 --> 00:08:42.120
Share your life with them
and never let them go.

123
00:08:53.740 --> 00:08:56.180
[SCHOLARS]
This is it. We're done for!

124
00:08:56.180 --> 00:08:59.950
[DR. CLOVER]
So this is the history
that mankind has chosen.

125
00:08:59.950 --> 00:09:03.350
Shall we ever learn
the error of our ways?

126
00:09:04.170 --> 00:09:07.910
[NICO OLIVIA]
Forgive me Robin.

127
00:09:08.210 --> 00:09:12.080
I couldn't even leave you
with any parting words.

128
00:09:12.080 --> 00:09:16.090
Neither as a scholar, or a mother.

129
00:09:16.520 --> 00:09:19.520
[SCHOLARS]
The Tree of Knowledge, it's falling!

130
00:09:27.490 --> 00:09:29.440
[KUZAN]
The concept of "absolute justice"

131
00:09:29.440 --> 00:09:32.700
can sometimes drive a man to madness.

132
00:09:32.700 --> 00:09:34.570
I've decided to let you escape.

133
00:09:34.570 --> 00:09:37.140
I'm curious to see what
kind of flower will sprout

134
00:09:37.140 --> 00:09:39.540
from the seed that Saul protected.

135
00:09:39.540 --> 00:09:40.770
You can bear a grudge against

136
00:09:40.770 --> 00:09:45.280
whoever you like for this but
at least you're still alive.

137
00:09:45.280 --> 00:09:49.390
However, I do suggest
you keep a low profile.

138
00:09:49.390 --> 00:09:52.640
I've drawn a path for you
on the sea with my ice.

139
00:09:52.640 --> 00:09:56.950
If you take the boat and go straight
ahead, you'll reach land eventually.

140
00:09:56.950 --> 00:10:00.380
Oh, one last thing.

141
00:10:00.380 --> 00:10:05.170
I'm not your ally. If you do
cause any trouble,

142
00:10:05.170 --> 00:10:08.570
I'll be the first
person to come after you.

143
00:10:08.570 --> 00:10:10.910
My mom's here, can you help her?

144
00:10:10.910 --> 00:10:12.880
[KUZAN]
No one will be saved.

145
00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:17.620
If that pain is too great for you
to bear, then you may join them.

146
00:10:17.620 --> 00:10:20.600
[DR. CLOVER]
This library is the best in the world!

147
00:10:20.600 --> 00:10:23.040
Do you like to read books?

148
00:10:23.040 --> 00:10:25.290
[DR. CLOVER]
Today is Robin's birthday!

149
00:10:25.290 --> 00:10:28.590
[EVERYONE]
Happy birthday from us at the library!

150
00:10:28.590 --> 00:10:30.260
[SAUL]
Your mamma's a wonderful woman!

151
00:10:30.260 --> 00:10:32.160
Ohara's a wonderful place!

152
00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:34.630
And as surely as we
believe in the past,

153
00:10:34.630 --> 00:10:37.640
we believe in the future
that you will inherit!

154
00:10:37.640 --> 00:10:39.490
When you're feelin' down, just laugh.

155
00:10:39.490 --> 00:10:41.850
There ain't nothin'
a good laugh can't fix.

156
00:10:42.610 --> 00:10:45.080
[ROBIN]
It seems awfully silly
to laugh when you're sad.

157
00:10:45.080 --> 00:10:46.950
[SAUL]
Don't knock it till you try it!

158
00:11:22.140 --> 00:11:26.650
[SAUL]
The sea's a vast place,
so I guarantee someday you'll find friends

159
00:11:26.650 --> 00:11:27.650
who won't ever leave you!

160
00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:48.200
[MARINE]
Survivors? No, I don't think so.

161
00:11:49.410 --> 00:11:50.170
[MARINE]
Hey!

162
00:11:50.170 --> 00:11:50.840
Huh?

163
00:11:50.840 --> 00:11:53.180
[MARINE]
Come here, look at the lake!

164
00:11:53.180 --> 00:11:55.750
What? That's insane!

165
00:12:01.710 --> 00:12:04.020
How did all of those books get here?

166
00:12:04.020 --> 00:12:06.690
[MARINE]
It can't be a coincidence!

167
00:12:06.690 --> 00:12:10.130
[SPANDINE]
Yeah, this is her!
That's definitely the girl!

168
00:12:10.130 --> 00:12:12.260
Where did you find her?
Is she captured?

169
00:12:12.260 --> 00:12:15.690
[MARINE]
No, we were told to keep
watch for a suspicious girl.

170
00:12:15.690 --> 00:12:18.700
We eventually found her on
a passenger ship Northeast of Ohara.

171
00:12:18.700 --> 00:12:20.700
Unfortunately,
she knew what we were after,

172
00:12:20.700 --> 00:12:23.430
so she slipped away
before we could catch her.

173
00:12:23.430 --> 00:12:25.770
[SPANDINE]
She's got the devil's luck.

174
00:12:25.770 --> 00:12:28.340
Back then, I'm sure
I saw her leaving Ohara.

175
00:12:28.340 --> 00:12:30.140
The island was burning to ash,

176
00:12:30.140 --> 00:12:33.170
but she somehow made it out
alone on a little rowboat!

177
00:12:33.170 --> 00:12:35.980
Of course, I tried to chase
her but all of a sudden,

178
00:12:35.980 --> 00:12:38.830
the helm of our boat got
stuck like it was frozen in ice!

179
00:12:38.830 --> 00:12:42.100
Either way, Saul probably helped
her escape before he died.

180
00:12:42.390 --> 00:12:44.890
[SENGOKU]
A scholar with the ability
to read the Poneglyphs

181
00:12:44.890 --> 00:12:47.920
is dangerous no matter
how young she may be.

182
00:12:49.260 --> 00:12:51.330
I don't care what methods you use.

183
00:12:51.330 --> 00:12:53.230
If we don't capture her immediately,

184
00:12:53.230 --> 00:12:56.660
then this entire mission
will have been for nothing!

185
00:12:59.880 --> 00:13:01.270
[MAN]
79 million Berries?

186
00:13:01.270 --> 00:13:04.640
[MAN]
Why does an eight-year-old
child have such a high bounty?

187
00:13:05.160 --> 00:13:07.670
[MAN]
They said she's one
of the devils of Ohara.

188
00:13:07.670 --> 00:13:10.110
You know, those scholars who
were plotting to end the world.

189
00:13:10.110 --> 00:13:12.030
[MAN]
Really?

190
00:13:12.030 --> 00:13:14.770
[MAN]
I heard she sank six
Marine battleships, too.

191
00:13:14.770 --> 00:13:17.110
She must have some kind of weird power.

192
00:13:17.110 --> 00:13:19.450
Well, that explains the bounty.

193
00:13:19.450 --> 00:13:23.020
[MAN]
The government forces and Navy
leaders are searching for her, too!

194
00:13:23.020 --> 00:13:27.160
[MAN]
She probably wants to carry out the same
plan as the scholars that were executed.

195
00:13:27.160 --> 00:13:30.390
If she's out for revenge,
then no one is safe!

196
00:13:30.850 --> 00:13:34.020
[MAN]
We can't let a child
of the devil run wild!

197
00:13:34.020 --> 00:13:35.820
[WOMAN]
Such a kind girl.

198
00:13:35.820 --> 00:13:37.290
Thank you for helping me out.

199
00:13:37.290 --> 00:13:40.290
Sure! I'm grateful
for any work I can get.

200
00:13:40.290 --> 00:13:45.260
[WOMAN]
By the way, before we have our
dinner some men are here to see you.

201
00:13:46.350 --> 00:13:47.820
[OFFICIAL]
Don't let her get away!

202
00:13:47.820 --> 00:13:49.190
[WOMAN]
Now, give me my money!

203
00:13:49.190 --> 00:13:51.710
I told you where she
was hiding, didn't I?

204
00:13:51.710 --> 00:13:55.040
[WOMAN]
She may be small,
but she still works hard.

205
00:13:56.910 --> 00:13:57.900
[MAN]
What's wrong?

206
00:13:57.900 --> 00:13:59.130
Having trouble sleeping?

207
00:13:59.130 --> 00:14:02.740
We have to get up early tomorrow
to go to work, so rest well.

208
00:14:02.740 --> 00:14:04.080
'Kay.

209
00:14:04.080 --> 00:14:07.720
[MAN]
She's sweet but if we keep her around,
we could get in serious trouble.

210
00:14:08.410 --> 00:14:11.350
Besides, just look at this bounty!

211
00:14:11.650 --> 00:14:14.060
[WOMAN]
Honey, she isn't in her room!

212
00:14:14.060 --> 00:14:14.890
[MAN]
Damn it!

213
00:14:14.890 --> 00:14:16.790
She must've overheard us talking!

214
00:14:21.850 --> 00:14:23.920
[ROBIN]
Dereshishishi!

215
00:14:23.920 --> 00:14:27.160
You're hungry? Sorry. Me too.

216
00:14:32.420 --> 00:14:35.850
[CAPTAIN]
Seems we're both
wanted by the law, Robin.

217
00:14:35.850 --> 00:14:38.860
I know all about you.

218
00:14:38.860 --> 00:14:42.120
Work for me and I'll make
sure you never go hungry.

219
00:14:43.370 --> 00:14:44.070
[CREWMEN]
Captain!

220
00:14:44.770 --> 00:14:46.100
The Marines are after us!

221
00:14:46.100 --> 00:14:47.360
Where did Robin go?

222
00:14:47.360 --> 00:14:48.960
Hand her over, damn it!

223
00:14:48.960 --> 00:14:52.230
Hurry! That girl is bad luck!

224
00:14:54.770 --> 00:14:57.840
[WOMAN]
A devil like you shouldn't even exist!

225
00:14:58.290 --> 00:15:00.830
[MAN]
What? Nico Robin's here? Where at?

226
00:15:00.830 --> 00:15:01.930
[MAN]
Hunt her down!

227
00:15:01.930 --> 00:15:03.630
Turn her in to the government!

228
00:15:07.970 --> 00:15:11.410
[ROBIN]
I can't believe it. A Poneglyph.

229
00:15:11.410 --> 00:15:12.410
[SHOPKEEPER]
Stay away!

230
00:15:12.410 --> 00:15:15.410
I have nothing to
sell to the likes of you!

231
00:15:15.410 --> 00:15:17.940
Look, I'm 16. I'll do anything.

232
00:15:17.940 --> 00:15:20.250
Please, just allow
me to join your group.

233
00:15:20.250 --> 00:15:22.860
[THUG]
You betrayed me, you damn witch!

234
00:15:24.080 --> 00:15:25.920
[CROCODILE]
Nico Robin.

235
00:15:25.920 --> 00:15:28.220
I'd like you to assist me.

236
00:15:29.820 --> 00:15:33.420
I've been told you can read Poneglyphs.

237
00:15:36.360 --> 00:15:41.730
[ROBIN]
If you trigger a Buster Call,
everything will be destroyed.

238
00:15:43.070 --> 00:15:46.580
That includes all of Enies Lobby,

239
00:15:47.890 --> 00:15:50.930
and most likely you as well.

240
00:15:50.930 --> 00:15:53.100
[SPANDAM]
Nonsense! What're you saying?

241
00:15:53.100 --> 00:15:55.960
They wouldn't kill a VIP like me!

242
00:15:55.960 --> 00:15:57.510
I'm not falling for your bluff!

243
00:15:57.510 --> 00:16:01.440
20 years ago, everything
was taken from me.

244
00:16:02.300 --> 00:16:04.510
And many innocent lives were lost.

245
00:16:05.370 --> 00:16:10.060
With one push of a button,
they summoned a terrible demon.

246
00:16:10.060 --> 00:16:12.250
Now it rears its head again.

247
00:16:12.250 --> 00:16:16.500
Aiming its sights on the friends
I've searched so hard to find.

248
00:16:16.500 --> 00:16:19.240
The more that I wish
for us to be together,

249
00:16:19.240 --> 00:16:23.610
the more my ugly fate
bares its fangs at you!

250
00:16:23.610 --> 00:16:29.990
Even now, no matter how far we sail,
there's an enemy that haunts me at every turn!

251
00:16:29.990 --> 00:16:34.220
Because I'm facing the world,
and all of its darkness.

252
00:16:34.220 --> 00:16:37.890
First it was Aokiji, and now CP9.

253
00:16:37.890 --> 00:16:41.160
I've dragged you into
my troubles twice already!

254
00:16:41.430 --> 00:16:46.710
If it goes on and on like this,
no matter how kind you may be,

255
00:16:46.710 --> 00:16:48.850
someday, you'll see me as a burden.

256
00:16:49.600 --> 00:16:53.020
Someday you'll be forced to
betray me and throw me away!

257
00:16:53.020 --> 00:16:55.000
That's what I'm most afraid of!

258
00:16:55.000 --> 00:16:58.140
Understand? That's why
I didn't want you to rescue me!

259
00:16:58.140 --> 00:17:03.440
If that's the only future I have,
I'd rather die to save me the pain!

260
00:17:07.680 --> 00:17:08.540
[CHOPPER]
Robin.

261
00:17:08.540 --> 00:17:10.310
I never knew.

262
00:17:11.520 --> 00:17:13.150
[NAMI]
Robin.

263
00:17:14.020 --> 00:17:16.320
[ZORO]
I see. So that's it.

264
00:17:18.970 --> 00:17:20.140
There you have it!

265
00:17:20.140 --> 00:17:22.140
Yep! Right on the mark!

266
00:17:22.140 --> 00:17:23.140
What a sorry case!

267
00:17:23.140 --> 00:17:27.210
Even if you make friends, all you can do
is drag them through the mud with you!

268
00:17:29.320 --> 00:17:32.290
You can't win, pirates!
Look at this flag!

269
00:17:34.750 --> 00:17:38.860
This symbol represents the
unity of over 170 nations.

270
00:17:38.860 --> 00:17:42.390
A power that spans the
four seas and the Grand Line!

271
00:17:42.390 --> 00:17:44.900
This is the world itself!

272
00:17:44.900 --> 00:17:48.570
No matter how loud your bark may be,
you can't stand up to an enemy like that!

273
00:17:48.570 --> 00:17:50.100
Just face it already!

274
00:17:50.100 --> 00:17:52.970
Do you realize how
strong our organization is?

275
00:17:52.970 --> 00:17:56.310
Do you realize how devoted
we are to capturing her?

276
00:17:56.930 --> 00:17:59.900
[LUFFY]
If that's Robin's enemy,
then I know what to do.

277
00:17:59.900 --> 00:18:01.140
Sniper King.

278
00:18:01.140 --> 00:18:02.770
[SOGEKING]
Hm?

279
00:18:03.040 --> 00:18:05.540
Shoot down that flag.

280
00:18:05.540 --> 00:18:07.330
[SOGEKING]
Roger.

281
00:18:07.330 --> 00:18:11.770
[SOGEKING]
This my new weapon, a massive
slingshot by the name of Kabuto!

282
00:18:12.850 --> 00:18:15.100
Behold its awesome power!

283
00:18:15.100 --> 00:18:18.900
Special Attack Firebird Star!

284
00:18:26.800 --> 00:18:28.400
No way.

285
00:18:31.240 --> 00:18:32.940
[SOGEKING]
Mission complete.

286
00:18:36.470 --> 00:18:38.040
[MARINE]
Now they've done it!

287
00:18:38.040 --> 00:18:39.140
Those idiots!

288
00:18:39.140 --> 00:18:42.780
[MARINE]
You can't fire on a
government flag! That's crazy!

289
00:18:43.370 --> 00:18:48.710
Those pirates just declared war
against the World Government!

290
00:18:48.710 --> 00:18:49.970
You're all going to die!

291
00:18:49.970 --> 00:18:53.980
You morons can't challenge the
entire world and expect to win!

292
00:18:53.980 --> 00:18:54.680
[LUFFY]
Yeah?

293
00:18:54.680 --> 00:18:59.050
Bring it on!

294
00:19:08.520 --> 00:19:11.610
Robin!

295
00:19:11.610 --> 00:19:15.880
There's still something
I want to hear you say!

296
00:19:18.410 --> 00:19:23.320
Tell me you want to live!

297
00:19:25.830 --> 00:19:26.960
Robin.

298
00:19:31.500 --> 00:19:32.700
Robin.

299
00:19:35.070 --> 00:19:37.070
[ROBIN]
I can live?

300
00:19:37.070 --> 00:19:38.040
Face it!

301
00:19:38.040 --> 00:19:40.980
[MAN]
Your whole existence
is nothing but a crime!

302
00:19:40.980 --> 00:19:43.020
[MAN]
The whole world's against you Robin!

303
00:19:43.020 --> 00:19:45.830
You can't be allowed to live!

304
00:19:46.410 --> 00:19:49.550
[ROBIN]
I never dared to wish
for something like that.

305
00:19:52.230 --> 00:19:55.800
The world had denied me that hope.

306
00:19:55.800 --> 00:19:58.870
I just want to die!

307
00:19:58.870 --> 00:20:02.710
[SAUL]
The sea's a vast place so I guarantee...

308
00:20:03.750 --> 00:20:07.650
someday you'll find friends
who won't ever leave you!

309
00:20:11.730 --> 00:20:14.000
[SOGEKING]
Believe in Luffy.

310
00:20:20.060 --> 00:20:20.760
But now.

311
00:20:20.760 --> 00:20:27.770
[ROBIN]
If I'm allowed to say my
wish...just this once. Then I...

312
00:20:28.120 --> 00:20:32.730
I want to live! Take me with you!

313
00:20:33.020 --> 00:20:35.960
Take me away from here!

314
00:20:59.750 --> 00:21:00.950
[FRANKY]
You guys!

315
00:21:00.950 --> 00:21:04.220
You're so awesome...I love you!

316
00:21:05.220 --> 00:21:06.460
[LUFFY]
Let's go!
